---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.author}.`}>
	<h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-3xl">About</h1>
	<div class="prose dark:prose-invert mt-6 max-w-none">
		<p>
			Hi, I'm David — an Azure Cloud Architect at glueckkanja AG, based in Bavaria, Germany.
			Colleagues started calling me Data Dave; the name stuck, and eventually it became this blog.
		</p>
		<p>
			For the last several years I've worked on the unglamorous but essential part of the stack: the
			data foundation — pulling scattered sources into a single lakehouse, structuring it, cleaning
			it up, and making it something teams can actually build on.
		</p>
		<p>
			That foundation is what separates AI that works from AI that demos well. LLMs, agents, and
			automation only earn their keep when the data underneath them holds — otherwise they're just
			confident hallucination. This blog covers that intersection: field lessons from real Azure
			data &amp; AI engagements — what worked, what broke, and what I'd do differently. No theory
			for theory's sake.
		</p>
		<p>
			Away from the keyboard I play guitar and trombone, sing in a choir, and poke at new tools
			mostly to find out what they're actually good for — which, honestly, is how half of these
			posts will start. Opinions here are my own, not my employer's. If something here sparks a
			question, the footer knows where to find me.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
